diff --git a/docs/layertree.md b/docs/layertree.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..a755fcc5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/layertree.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# Experimental LayerTree MID backend
+
+This branch implements the four opcode extensions needed to run LayerTree's
+MID covenant scripts on a private regtest chain. Based on the reference
+implementation at lightninglabs/layertree commit
+`f64cc0e4d4471e32f7fd8294ecb0b1c7547c1166`.
+
+```sh
+go build -o btcd .
+./btcd --regtest --experimental-layertree
+```
+
+Use a new data directory and explicit RPC configuration. The accompanying
+LayerTree `mvp/run.sh` handles those details and exercises the backend.
+
+The flag applies the same rules to mempool validation, block template
+construction and block connection. It is rejected outside regtest. The
+library also guards the network when constructing a blockchain instance.
+Standard Bitcoin behavior is unchanged when the flag is absent.
+
+## Opcodes
+
+* `OP_CAT` at `0x7e`: concatenate two elements, bounded to 520 bytes.
+* `OP_TX` at `0xbf`: selectors `0x8000`, `0x10800`, `0x20800` and `0x4300`.
+  These expose the current input number, current spent amount, current spent
+  scriptPubKey and a selected output's amount and scriptPubKey. Amounts are
+  eight-byte little-endian values. Indexes are Script numbers. Other draft
+  selectors fail closed.
+* `OP_TWEAKADD` at `0xc0`: x-only public key plus a scalar times G. Rejects
+  malformed operands, invalid points, scalar overflow and infinity. Costs
+  50 signature budget units.
+* `OP_CHECKSIGFROMSTACK` at `0xcc`: BIP340 signature verification over a
+  message from the stack. Supports variable-length messages. A nonempty
+  signature costs 50 signature budget units.
+
+These are enabled only in tapscript leaf version `0xc0`. The opcode bytes
+match the LayerTree simulator's placeholders, including its resolutions of
+conflicting draft assignments. This does not implement all `OP_TX` selectors,
+FULL restored arithmetic, CCV or hypothetical native Merkle-sum operations.
+
+The existing 520-byte element, 1,000-element stack, four-byte numeric and
+BIP342 signature budgets remain active. The opcode-success pre-scan recognizes
+the four restored opcodes and executes their semantics. Other upgradeable
+opcodes and leaf versions retain their existing behavior.
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+go test ./txscript ./blockchain ./mempool ./mining
+```
+
+`txscript/layertree_test.go` exercises valid and invalid operands, oversized
+concatenation, input and output introspection, scalar and point failures,
+signature failures, budget exhaustion and activation boundaries. The CSV
+fixture is from bitcoin/bips `bip-0340/test-vectors.csv` and includes
+variable-length messages.
+
+The LayerTree checkout's `mvp/test.sh` also executes 104 reference MID cases
+through this interpreter and a real regtest lifecycle. The lifecycle includes
+a direct block submission with an invalid covenant, valid proof of work and
+a valid witness commitment, to verify enforcement beyond mempool policy.
